**Vulnerability Type:** Read-after-write conflicts (phantom reads)
**Severity:** Medium
**Affected Code Location:** `Query`, `Deposit`, `Withdraw`
**Description:** The chaincode does not handle concurrent transactions properly. If two transactions are executed simultaneously, it may lead to phantom reads where a transaction reads data that was not committed yet.
**Recommended Fix:** Use transactions to ensure that all operations are atomic and that no other transaction can interfere with the current transaction.

